# The game data and the annotation datasets are built into the binaries,
# fingerprinted (server.Data.Hash) and sent to models as they are: keep them
# LF in every checkout, Windows included, so that a game, a prompt and an
# annotation run are the same on every machine. The documents too, since
# tests and checks compare some of them byte for byte with the data (the
# batch-2 copies, walton-clean). The fingerprints read CRLF as LF anyway,
# and so do annotation runs' pinned inputs; a checkout made before this
# file keeps its line endings until its files are written again.
wag/data/** text=auto eol=lf
docs/** text=auto eol=lf
